WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.290
In 1526, William Tyndale's English
New Testament used the word atonement.

2
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.500
Break it apart, and it means at-one-ment:

3
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.150
making one again.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.570
Christians believe sin
separates humans from God,

5
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.980
and that God offers forgiveness
through Jesus' death.

6
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:22.890
Yet the creeds say Christ died for
us, without explaining how that works.

7
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:28.600
So how could one death, long ago, put
things right between God and everyone else?

8
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.720
In this mission, you'll follow Anselm's
famous argument about honour and debt.

9
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.760
Then you'll weigh up a sharp charge:
does any of this make God cruel?

10
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: find out how Christians
have explained the power of the cross.
